  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cross-Border Conflict, Evidence, Policy and Trends (XCEPT) Research Programme, Lot 1.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the programme is to improve effectiveness of HMG investments in fragile and conflict affected situations (FCAS), by providing real-time data, expertise and public good research to inform FCDO and Whitehall policy and operations including through the Whitehall Conflict Security and Stability Fund (CSSF) and FCDO programmes. The programme is broken into two separate contracts: Lot 1 (cross-border conflict dynamics/response), and Lot 2 (violent and peaceful behaviour). This contract is Lot 1 which examines how conflicts connect across borders. It is led by Chemonics and Chatham House with Conciliation Resources, and support from specialist partner Satellite Applications Catapult. Research revolves around case studies of cross-border conflict dynamics spanning the Middle East and North Africa, the Sahel and the Horn of Africa, and South Asia. The XCEPT Research Fund also enables responsive research on emerging conflicts and supports international and local researchers to build evidence on what works to stabilise, resolve and prevent conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
